{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head c98b9a2cad5c66414ffe54c97d8862e4d5a02f6d on planner/client-primitive-note-20261113, its one artifact `notes/2026-11-13-scope-client.md`, for request e5b86654 under promise 52171349 and review request fded66e1. The head answers verdict 2123f760, and its one commit since f0854d8f changes only the parts that the verdict named.\n\nWhat I read, since f0854d8f:\n\n- The required change. Section 5.1 now checks both bounds before custody signs. A record that holds 8 envelopes or 64 signings refuses a further signing with `full`, reason `signings`, signs nothing, and keeps the member's values in the draft. Custody drops no envelope, and the note gives the reason: the scope can seal the signing of each envelope that is not closed. A signing closes at the latest at a read after its death (5.3, 5.4), so the member can submit again. Ruling 72b1d654 carries the rule to C1.\n- Section 10 now names its subject: the new member on `mismatch` needs `docs/kernel.md` section 7, and the note does not take it. My kernel reading in 2123f760 stands. The note changes no answer shape and names no K item.\n- Section 5.3 now states which envelopes a `refused` record keeps, and that the store keeps it as it keeps each terminal record. C1 and NF-5 state that bound for each store. That answers my first note.\n- Rules 3 and 4 of section 6 stay two rules, because Hugh ratified six. I accept that.\n- The status line records that the review added the rule of 5.1 after the ratification.\n\nWhat I checked: main 57e893c0 is an ancestor, and the head changes one path. The artifact covers it at the head and is neither stale nor retired. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, the commit-message check passes (7 checked, 0 flagged), and `git diff --check` is clean.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The conclusions of 2123f760 stand, and the bound now holds at the point where custody signs.\n\nSecurity: no finding. No envelope that the scope can still seal leaves custody, so a `mismatch` settle reads every signing that can hold the key.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nThis approval authorizes no landing. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f887ed9e4bbdfd1df71a83aa9e3727e4bee36daf","binding":"assigned","head":"c98b9a2cad5c66414ffe54c97d8862e4d5a02f6d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:59e975f1df8cedc705b6048cb47ce550d1b5291f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:52171349a1a04f8ff2d60672c3d60dd527614b20\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:59e975f1df8cedc705b6048cb47ce550d1b5291f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}